+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-replace-in-place/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+## Why
+
+`replace` is implemented as `remove` followed by `add`. On an object member this moves the member to the end of the object instead of replacing it in place, which surprises users.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `replace` sets the value at the existing target in place: an object member keeps its position, an array element keeps its index.
+- Error behaviour is unchanged (missing target, `-` index, invalid pointers).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: the `replace` requirement states in-place replacement.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/json-patch.ts` (`replace` case) and `test/json-patch.test.ts`.
